Map whole-file reads on Linux

Swift 6's Linux Foundation does not map files for .mappedIfSafe. Every
whole-file Data(contentsOf:options:) is a malloc and a full read, where
Darwin gets a lazy mmap. models import opens the safetensors twice before
printing Detected, and the server's two SHA-256 paths and GRPCFileUploader
each read whole checkpoints into memory.

Data.ReadingOptions.mappedIfLocal is .mappedIfSafe on Darwin and
.alwaysMapped on Linux, which FoundationEssentials implements with a real
mmap. Darwin behaviour is unchanged.
